# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# ctags
tags

# Go build output.
#
# /cmd is the trap that actually caught us: `go build ./services/seeder/...` names
# its output after the LAST PATH ELEMENT, so every service in this repo compiles to
# a binary called "cmd" in the working directory. A `git add -A` then commits 25M of
# ELF to a public repo without anybody noticing, which is exactly what happened in
# c48a869 on 2026-08-27. Anchored with a leading slash so services/*/cmd/ - the
# actual source directories - stay tracked.
/cmd
tmp/
main
*.out
out.html

# NOTE: /.github/ here is THIS repo's CI directory and is tracked.
# The `reeldex` GitHub org profile repo that used to live at this path was moved to
# ../reeldex-dotgithub on 2026-08-24 — it is a separate repo for a separate org, and
# GitHub requires workflows to live at .github/workflows/, so the two cannot share
# the path.
